  "prefLabel": "Ed 1113.07 Prohibition on Mandatory Medication",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1113.07 Prohibition on Mandatory Medication. As provided in 34 CFR 300.174, an LEA, other public agency, private provider of special education or other non-LEA program shall not require parents to\n\nobtain a prescription for substances identified under schedules I, II, III, IV, or V in section 202(c) of the Controlled Substance Act, 21 U.S.C. 812(c), for a child as a condition of attending school, receiving an evaluation, or receiving services.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
}
